dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.unary.op]/9: "The operand of the logical negation operator ! is
contextually converted to bool"; [conv.array] + [conv.bool]: a string
literal converts to a non-null pointer and so to true.  The front end
rejects `!"literal"' ("invalid implicit conversion from 'const char [17l]'
to '__CPROVER_bool'").  libstdc++'s regex scanner uses exactly this in
`__glibcxx_assert(!"unexpected state while processing regex")'
(regex_scanner.tcc:86), dropping _Scanner::_M_advance / _M_scan_normal
(regex_scanner.h:222/239) in the regex descs of the round-163 audit.
Header-free.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 fails the same way).
